1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,390
Last time, we made an electromagnet by the electrical method.

2
00:00:04,870 --> 00:00:07,700
Take the battery away, and the clips drop off.

3
00:00:12,899 --> 00:00:15,409
A little cricket is hiding in this video.

4
00:00:15,659 --> 00:00:16,889
Can you spot it?

5
00:00:17,018 --> 00:00:18,858
Lock in first with your fingers.

6
00:00:19,128 --> 00:00:20,958
One finger for every point.

7
00:00:21,545 --> 00:00:22,875
Today you'll learn:

8
00:00:23,075 --> 00:00:24,605
More turns of wire.

9
00:00:24,810 --> 00:00:26,110
More batteries.

10
00:00:26,310 --> 00:00:28,200
Iron and steel, not wood.

11
00:00:29,805 --> 00:00:30,685
Round one.

12
00:00:30,995 --> 00:00:34,865
Momo's nail has ten turns of wire, and Basil's has twenty.

13
00:00:35,135 --> 00:00:36,595
Each has one battery.

14
00:00:36,865 --> 00:00:39,085
Which nail attracts more steel clips?

15
00:00:39,385 --> 00:00:40,675
One, ten turns.

16
00:00:40,945 --> 00:00:42,385
Two, twenty turns.

17
00:00:42,655 --> 00:00:44,085
Three, both the same.

18
00:00:44,375 --> 00:00:45,735
Show me your fingers.

19
00:00:51,206 --> 00:00:52,186
Locked in!

20
00:00:52,314 --> 00:00:53,184
Three.

21
00:00:53,344 --> 00:00:58,124
They both have one battery, and only batteries make an electromagnet stronger.

22
00:00:58,174 --> 00:00:58,814
Two!

23
00:00:58,954 --> 00:01:00,764
More turns is like more strokes.

24
00:01:00,864 --> 00:01:02,204
More turns, more pull!

25
00:01:02,258 --> 00:01:06,668
Two. Every turn of wire helps a little, so twenty turns help more.

26
00:01:06,946 --> 00:01:08,236
Be a steel bolt!

27
00:01:08,516 --> 00:01:09,506
Shrink down.

28
00:01:09,786 --> 00:01:10,716
Quietly.

29
00:01:12,997 --> 00:01:16,527
You are a steel bolt in our mini scrapyard, the heaviest scrap

30
00:01:16,547 --> 00:01:17,227
of all.

31
00:01:18,017 --> 00:01:21,527
Aluminium ring-pulls and plastic caps lie around you.

32
00:01:22,057 --> 00:01:24,637
Momo's hook with ten turns comes down.

33
00:01:25,427 --> 00:01:28,187
You tip up a little, and then you slip back down.

34
00:01:28,707 --> 00:01:31,317
Here comes Basil's hook with twenty turns.

35
00:01:32,077 --> 00:01:34,287
You jump up, and cling to its tip!

36
00:01:35,057 --> 00:01:36,877
The ring-pulls stay behind.

37
00:01:38,532 --> 00:01:41,202
The answer is two: Basil's twenty turns!

38
00:01:41,462 --> 00:01:43,042
Did you show two fingers?

39
00:01:43,302 --> 00:01:44,681
Put one finger up!

40
00:01:44,701 --> 00:01:47,641
A turn of wire is one time the wire goes round the

41
00:01:47,661 --> 00:01:50,501
nail, such as the twenty turns round my nail!

42
00:01:51,229 --> 00:01:53,159
But it is the same battery.

43
00:01:53,369 --> 00:01:55,689
How can more turns make it stronger?

44
00:01:56,344 --> 00:01:57,494
Look closer.

45
00:01:58,054 --> 00:02:01,624
The same nails, the same wire, and one battery each.

46
00:02:02,194 --> 00:02:04,457
Only the number of turns is different.

47
00:02:04,477 --> 00:02:07,987
The nail with twenty turns attracts more steel clips.

48
00:02:08,567 --> 00:02:10,977
Each turn of wire adds a little more pull.

49
00:02:10,997 --> 00:02:14,877
The strength of an electromagnet is how strongly it pulls, such as

50
00:02:14,897 --> 00:02:17,107
how many steel clips it can attract!

51
00:02:17,681 --> 00:02:22,401
Our school bell has an electromagnet inside, with many turns of wire.

52
00:02:22,971 --> 00:02:26,681
It switches on and off very fast, so a little hammer hits

53
00:02:26,701 --> 00:02:28,261
the bell again and again!

54
00:02:30,969 --> 00:02:32,129
Say it with me!

55
00:02:32,835 --> 00:02:36,775
We can increase the strength of an electromagnet by increasing the number

56
00:02:36,795 --> 00:02:39,535
of turns of wire around the iron nail.

57
00:02:43,007 --> 00:02:43,917
Showdown!

58
00:02:44,217 --> 00:02:45,347
Double points.

59
00:02:45,617 --> 00:02:49,117
Momo's poster for Recycling Week has one mistake.

60
00:02:49,387 --> 00:02:51,167
Line one, two, or three?

61
00:02:51,457 --> 00:02:52,927
Show me with your fingers.

62
00:02:52,990 --> 00:02:55,470
One: coil a long wire round the iron nail.

63
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:57,780
Two: join both ends to the battery.

64
00:02:57,850 --> 00:03:02,070
Three: electricity is stronger, so a light wooden chopstick works too!

65
00:03:07,683 --> 00:03:08,663
Locked in!

66
00:03:08,791 --> 00:03:09,531
Three!

67
00:03:09,621 --> 00:03:13,951
A wooden chopstick cannot be made into a magnet, even with electricity.

68
00:03:14,261 --> 00:03:16,161
Wood is not a magnetic material.

69
00:03:17,038 --> 00:03:18,128
Three fingers?

70
00:03:18,368 --> 00:03:20,298
Put up two more on your score hand!

71
00:03:20,433 --> 00:03:24,413
Objects made of iron and steel can be made into magnets using

72
00:03:24,433 --> 00:03:27,293
the stroke method or the electrical method.

73
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:30,740
We have used up all our wire.

74
00:03:30,980 --> 00:03:33,170
How else can we make our crane stronger?

75
00:03:33,819 --> 00:03:34,969
Look closer.

76
00:03:35,549 --> 00:03:37,859
Two nails, each with twenty turns.

77
00:03:38,429 --> 00:03:40,509
One is joined to one battery.

78
00:03:41,079 --> 00:03:44,090
The other is joined to two batteries, in a row.

79
00:03:44,110 --> 00:03:47,630
The nail with two batteries attracts more steel clips.

80
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:51,578
More batteries make more electricity flow round the coil.

81
00:03:51,598 --> 00:03:55,158
The number of batteries is how many batteries we join together, such

82
00:03:55,178 --> 00:03:57,998
as one battery, or two batteries in a row!

83
00:04:01,219 --> 00:04:02,019
Watch!

84
00:04:02,299 --> 00:04:05,529
Our crane carries the steel bolt to the lorry, and drops it

85
00:04:05,549 --> 00:04:06,099
in!

86
00:04:06,761 --> 00:04:07,981
Say it with me!

87
00:04:08,692 --> 00:04:12,682
We can also increase the strength of an electromagnet by increasing the

88
00:04:12,702 --> 00:04:14,402
number of batteries used.

89
00:04:17,161 --> 00:04:18,266
Say it with us!

90
00:04:18,926 --> 00:04:20,336
More turns of wire?

91
00:04:20,506 --> 00:04:22,256
A stronger electromagnet!

92
00:04:25,326 --> 00:04:26,505
More batteries?

93
00:04:26,906 --> 00:04:28,656
A stronger electromagnet!

94
00:04:31,726 --> 00:04:33,044
The wall socket?

95
00:04:33,306 --> 00:04:35,056
Never! Batteries only!

96
00:04:38,881 --> 00:04:40,341
Show me your score hand!

97
00:04:40,621 --> 00:04:42,071
Two fingers or more?

98
00:04:42,361 --> 00:04:43,721
You beat the Buddies.

99
00:04:44,011 --> 00:04:45,081
Three fingers?

100
00:04:45,361 --> 00:04:46,361
High five!

101
00:04:46,564 --> 00:04:48,054
Did you spot the cricket?

102
00:04:48,314 --> 00:04:50,934
It was on the ledge, right under the school bell!

103
00:04:51,064 --> 00:04:52,554
Here is a fun fact!

104
00:04:52,644 --> 00:04:56,254
A cricket's ears are on its front legs, just below its knees!

105
00:04:56,304 --> 00:04:58,964
So when our school bell rings, the cricket hears it with its

106
00:04:58,984 --> 00:04:59,844
legs!

107
00:04:59,965 --> 00:05:01,245
Tell someone at home!

108
00:05:02,184 --> 00:05:07,394
Next time: Basil tests which makes a stronger electromagnet, an iron nail

109
00:05:07,414 --> 00:05:08,654
or a steel nail.

110
00:05:08,924 --> 00:05:13,104
He coils twenty-five turns round the iron nail, but only eight turns

111
00:05:13,124 --> 00:05:14,294
round the steel nail.

112
00:05:14,584 --> 00:05:15,764
Is his test fair?

113
00:05:16,054 --> 00:05:17,144
One, yes.

114
00:05:17,414 --> 00:05:18,274
Two, no.

115
00:05:18,554 --> 00:05:19,864
Lock in your answer!

116
00:05:20,142 --> 00:05:22,342
Let's read today's key words together!

117
00:05:22,632 --> 00:05:23,392
Ready?

118
00:05:23,679 --> 00:05:24,809
Turns of wire.

119
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:27,280
Strength.

120
00:05:28,625 --> 00:05:30,055
Number of batteries.

121
00:05:31,887 --> 00:05:32,827
Well done!

122
00:05:33,809 --> 00:05:34,910
Say it with us!

123
00:05:35,710 --> 00:05:36,460
Ready?

124
00:05:36,583 --> 00:05:37,243
One!

125
00:05:37,583 --> 00:05:38,283
two!

126
00:05:38,588 --> 00:05:39,763
Now you know!
